[32m+[m[32m# LedgerPoint — Secure Cloud File Storage Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Project:** TECHCRUSH Group 2 — Secure Cloud File Storage System[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Cloud Provider:** Microsoft Azure[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Architecture Status:** Proposed — pending final review and implementation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Architecture Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLedgerPoint requires a secure, affordable cloud file storage system that allows authorized employees to manage financial statements and share individual documents with external auditors without requiring auditor accounts.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe proposed solution uses Azure Blob Storage, Microsoft Entra ID, Azure RBAC, Bash, Azure CLI, user delegation SAS URLs, and audit logging.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Architecture Diagram[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```mermaid[m
[32m+[m[32mflowchart TD[m
[32m+[m[32m    E["Authorized LedgerPoint Employee"][m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI["Bash CLI - ledgerpoint.sh"][m
[32m+[m[32m    ID["Microsoft Entra ID / Azure RBAC"][m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    subgraph AZURE["Microsoft Azure"][m
[32m+[m[32m        STORAGE["Azure Storage Account"][m
[32m+[m[32m        ORIGINAL["Private Container: originals"][m
[32m+[m[32m        SHARED["Private Container: temporary-shares"][m
[32m+[m[32m        KEY["Azure Storage User Delegation Key"][m
[32m+[m[32m        DIAG["Storage Diagnostic Settings"][m
[32m+[m[32m        MONITOR["Log Analytics Workspace"][m
[32m+[m[32m    end[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    SAS["Temporary Read-Only SAS URL"][m
[32m+[m[32m    AUDITOR["External Auditor - No Login"][m
[32m+[m[32m    APPLOG["Application Audit Log"][m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    E --> CLI[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Authenticate and authorize"| ID[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Upload, list, download, delete"| ORIGINAL[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Create or revoke temporary copy"| SHARED[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    ORIGINAL --- STORAGE[m
[32m+[m[32m    SHARED --- STORAGE[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Request delegation key"| KEY[m
[32m+[m[32m    KEY -->|"Delegation key returned"| CLI[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Generate file-specific SAS"| SAS[m
[32m+[m[32m    SAS -->|"Securely provide link"| AUDITOR[m
[32m+[m[32m    AUDITOR -->|"HTTPS read request using SAS"| SHARED[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    CLI -->|"Record application actions"| APPLOG[m
[32m+[m[32m    STORAGE --> DIAG[m
[32m+[m[32m    DIAG --> MONITOR[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Component Responsibilities[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Component | Responsibility |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Authorized employee | Manages confidential documents through the Bash CLI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bash CLI | Handles file operations, sharing, revocation, validation, and application logging |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Microsoft Entra ID | Authenticates employee identities |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Azure RBAC | Grants only the permissions required for each operation |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Azure Storage Account | Hosts private Blob containers |[m
[32m+[m[32m| originals container | Preserves original confidential documents |[m
[32m+[m[32m| temporary-shares container | Holds uniquely named temporary copies intended for external sharing |[m
[32m+[m[32m| User Delegation SAS | Provides temporary, read-only authorization to a specific shared blob |[m
[32m+[m[32m| External auditor | Retrieves the permitted document without an Azure account |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Application audit log | Records user-initiated application actions |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Azure diagnostics | Records supported Blob Storage operations and request outcomes |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Log Analytics | Stores and supports investigation of Azure diagnostic events |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Document Upload Workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. An authorized employee signs in to Azure.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. The employee invokes the Bash CLI upload command.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. The CLI validates the request and checks the operation result.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. The document is uploaded into the private originals container.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. The application records the upload event.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. Azure Storage diagnostics provide additional evidence of the storage request.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Secure External Sharing Workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. An employee selects a document to share.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. The application creates a uniquely named temporary copy in the private temporary-shares container.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. The application obtains appropriate user delegation authorization from Azure Storage.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. A read-only, HTTPS-only SAS URL is generated for the temporary blob.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. The default expiry is 30 minutes, with a shorter configurable test duration.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. The application records the issuer, intended recipient, blob identifier, expiry, and result, without logging the SAS secret.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. The employee provides the URL to the intended auditor through an approved communication channel.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. The auditor accesses the temporary blob directly through Azure Storage.[m
[32m+[m[32m9. Azure Storage diagnostics can provide evidence of the access request.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 6. Expiry and Revocation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSAS access ends when its authorization expires.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor early revocation, an authorized employee invokes the application's revoke operation. The application identifies and deletes the corresponding temporary shared copy, preserving the original document.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach share must use a unique temporary blob name so that revoking one share does not unintentionally revoke another.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDeleting a temporary shared blob does not erase copies previously downloaded by the auditor.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExpired temporary copies must also be cleaned up.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 7. Security Controls[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Disable anonymous public Blob access.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep both Blob containers private.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use HTTPS for storage requests and shared URLs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Authenticate employees using Microsoft Entra ID.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Apply least-privilege Azure RBAC permissions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Prefer user delegation SAS instead of account-key-signed SAS.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Restrict external sharing to read-only access on a specific temporary blob.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Never commit credentials, SAS URLs, or confidential documents to Git.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Record successful and failed actions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Restrict access to application and Azure diagnostic logs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use synthetic financial documents during testing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 8. Audit Logging Design[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mApplication logs capture operations initiated through the Bash CLI, including who requested an action, the target resource, timestamp, and result.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAzure Storage diagnostic logs capture supported storage requests and help verify whether a file was accessed through a shared link.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mApplication audit records require secure storage or export beyond an ordinary editable local log file for a production-ready system. The implementation and retention controls will be validated during the logging stage.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA SAS download does not independently prove the real-world identity of the person using the URL. The intended recipient must be recorded separately.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 9. Cost and Operational Considerations[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe solution will use an economical Azure Storage configuration suitable for a small demonstration workload.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCosts must be monitored for storage capacity, storage transactions, and Azure Monitor / Log Analytics ingestion and retention.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTemporary files should be removed when no longer needed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Bash CLI should provide simple commands and understandable error messages so non-technical staff can operate it with minimal training.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 10. Architecture Verification Criteria[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe architecture will be considered implemented and verified when:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Both containers exist and anonymous public access is disabled.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Authenticated employees can perform authorized operations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The CLI supports upload, download, list, and delete.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A valid SAS URL permits the intended read operation without auditor login.[m
[32m+[m[32m- An expired SAS URL is denied.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Revoking a temporary shared copy prevents further normal retrieval through its SAS URL.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The original document remains intact after revocation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Application and Azure diagnostic logs provide evidence of operations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Automated deployment and end-to-end tests succeed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Final design approval:** Pending Phase 0 review.[m
